# skills

Skills for working with [SVN11X/standards](https://github.com/SVN11X/standards), version {{version}}. This repository is generated from the standards repository, so do not edit it by hand.

- `repo-setup`: create a repository or reorganize an existing one under the standard.
- `code-review`: review code or a pull request against the standard.

The skills follow the open Agent Skills format (a folder with a SKILL.md file), so the same folders work in Claude, Codex, Gemini CLI, GitHub Copilot, Cursor and other tools.

## Install in Claude

This covers claude.ai and Claude Code signed in with the same account.

1. Download `repo-setup.zip` and `code-review.zip` from the latest release of this repository.
2. In Claude, open Customize, then Skills.
3. Click +, then Create skill, then Upload a skill, and upload one ZIP. Repeat for the other.

Code execution must be on in Settings, Capabilities.

## Install in several agents at once

With Node.js installed, this installs into Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, GitHub Copilot, Cursor and others. It asks which agents to use.

```bash
npx skills add SVN11X/skills
```

## Install by hand

Copy each folder in `skills/` into the skills folder of your tool:

- Claude Code: `~/.claude/skills/`
- Codex: `~/.codex/skills/`
- Gemini CLI: `~/.gemini/skills/`
- GitHub Copilot: `~/.copilot/skills/`
- Cursor: `~/.cursor/skills/`
- One project only, for any of them: `.agents/skills/` inside the project.

## Update

Install again after each new release. The skills never download the standard at run time. Each one carries a copy pinned to the version in `skills/repo-setup/standard/VERSION`.
